{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794653366,"nonce":"eG47wiKoXXCW+GMS2NNKJgCy44I=","message":"Items 1 and 2 are built, not committed.\n\n1. `hxn::package!(\"window\");` in the crate puts every generated class, support classes included, in that package: under its directory, with a `package` line. Lowercase dotted parts, not `hxn`; declared once. The manifest gains `\"package\"` only when one is declared. `hxn build` and `hxn package` now keep nested class directories in step (they deleted only flat files before). `examples/picture` declares `picture` and runs in it.\n2. `hxn_gen::parse_crate_with(name, root, out_dir)` follows `include!(concat!(env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), \"/name.rs\"))`, asking for the directory once and only when it meets such an include. `hxn build` answers by running `cargo check` on the library (which runs its build script) and taking `out_dir` from the `build-script-executed` message whose `package_id` is what `cargo pkgid` prints. tests/cli now has the library made by `hxn new` write a function from its build script and call it.\n\nRun: tests/cli and tests/examples on Ash (hybrid), hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm, Emscripten; tests/counter gen-hl (Ash), gen-cpp, gen-cppia, gen-wasm, gen-emcc; cargo test, fmt, clippy. Not run: stock HashLink, Windows.\n\nWhat the x-idl target has to supply, from hlwindow's generated model: the model is plain Rust (`Event`, `OptionalText`, C-like enums, `Window { handle: i32 }`), and the backend's functions take it directly (`window_open(\u0026WindowAttributes) -\u003e i32`, `window_poll(i32) -\u003e Event`). Only descriptors hold runtime carriers (`Rooted\u003cText\u003e`, `Rooted\u003cBuffer\u003e`), from a `runtime` module that is `hl_xidl` for HashLink: about fifteen items (`Text`, `Buffer`, `BufferMut`, `Rooted`, `Rootable`, `Enum`, `NativeEnum`, `Future`, `Value`, `ErrorKind`, `host::raise`/`fail`/`throw_pending`/`agent`, `Managed`). The hxn target can emit the same model with hxn markers, wrappers calling the backend, and a plain-Rust carrier module over String, Vec\u003cu8\u003e and hxn-future; `host::raise` would record the message for the wrapper to return as an `Err` after the call.","files":null}]}